US-074 complete. Summary:

**Root cause (phase-01 hypothesis corrected):** The install-time failure was not generator ordering. Install → `applyManifestToWorkspace` → SDK client generation calls `createGraphQLSchema(workspace, applicationId)`, which filters flat maps to `[standard app, requested app]`. A2E Projects' `project.documents` targets A2E Documents' `document` object (a *different* application), so the filter kept the relation field but dropped its target → line-117 guard fired. The full (un-scoped) schema includes every object, which is why it "builds fine outside install"; the differing field id is just the per-attempt uuid.

**Fix (generic, guard untouched):** new `augmentFlatEntityMapsWithRelationTargets` pulls missing relation-target objects + their fields (transitively) from the full workspace maps into the app-scoped generation context. Wired into the `applicationId` branch only, so the normal workspace schema is unchanged.

**Changed:** `workspace-graphql-schema-sdl.service.ts`; new util + util spec; new service spec; phase-04 report; `.ralph-tui/progress.md`.

**Failing-then-passing:** util spec runs the real generator on the raw scoped context → throws the exact reported error; on the augmented context → builds. Service spec with the fix disabled → `Received: undefined` (target absent); restored → present.

**Checks:** new specs 5/5; `workspace-schema-builder` 22/22; `flat-entity` 66/66; `workspace-migration` 232/232; `tsgo --noEmit` exit 0; oxlint 0/0; oxfmt clean; `lint:diff-with-main` → "No changed files."; no `twenty-shared`/app-source/migration changes.

**Tier-2 residual (orchestrator):** live a2e-projects install re-proof → ticks M1a install leg and makes P4.1's concurrency proof runnable.

